WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.601
-The political world, including
a stunned and flailing Fox News,

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:07.267
is still reeling from
yesterday's shocking testimony

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:08.801
before the January 6th
Committee,

00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:10.801
in which former
Trump White House official

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:12.934
Cassidy Hutchinson
testified under oath

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:14.534
that, among other things,

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.167
President Trump
wanted his supporters

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:17.801
to be allowed into
his rally armed

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:20.067
so they could then march to
the Capitol with their weapons,

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:21.934
where he planned to meet them
and join the mob

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.734
in its effort
to overturn the election.

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:26.033
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:30.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:33.167
It's been a day and a half,
and honestly,

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:35.567
I'm still struggling
with words to fully capture

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:38.834
the gravity and insanity
of what we all heard yesterday.

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.934
In the first draft
of this script,

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:42.701
the intro for "A Closer Look"

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:45.400
was just a word
you can't say on TV.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.868
Wally, show them the card.

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:52.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:54.968
I think the moment
that best captures

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:57.300
just how stunned
everyone was yesterday

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.367
was this clip from
Fox News daytime anchors

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:01.467
shortly after the hearing ended.

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:04.067
The anchors tried to summarize
what had just happened,

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:05.334
and then when they were done,

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:07.868
they just sort of sat there
in awkward silence,

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:10.200
figuring out
whose turn it was to talk.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:13.000
-This testimony
was very compelling

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.434
from beginning to end.

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:17.300
She obviously had access
to all of the players.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.634
What was so compelling,
I think, is how it was laid out.

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:23.834
We always point out that there's
not a pushback,

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:26.167
and it would have been
great to hear Jim Jordan

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:30.067
or some congressman
say some other angle to this.

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:32.567
But the testimony in
and of itself

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:34.968
is really, really powerful.

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:40.467
[ Laughter ]
-Sandra, can you still hear?

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:43.834
-Indeed, yes, I am here.
-Oof!

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:46.367
That's like when you get
in the car with your parents

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:47.834
after they took you to a movie

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:50.634
that had way more nudity
than they were expecting.

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:52.400
"Well, uh...

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.634
when I heard it was [clears
throat] called 'Showgirls,'

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:57.434
I did expect it
would be a musical."

00:01:57.434 --> 00:01:59.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:02.167
I also like how they all
act like the question

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.367
was for the other person.

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:04.934
"John, why don't you go ahead?"

00:02:04.934 --> 00:02:07.667
"I'm sorry, are you talking to
me John or the cameraman John?"

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.567
"Sandra?
Do you want to take this one?"

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:12.100
"Oh, sorry, I couldn't hear you.
Why don't you go ahead, Bret?"

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.734
"No, no, no, no, no, no.
Ladies first."

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:18.067
The hearing was so powerful and
the revelations were so searing

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:20.000
that even
the opinion people on Fox

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.734
seemed knocked off their game.

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:23.334
They couldn't settle
on a coherent narrative

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:24.601
the way they usually do.

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:26.934
They just cycled through
a bunch of different lines,

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:28.501
from screaming about media bias

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:30.567
to claiming everyone knows
Trump gets angry

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:32.801
to dismissing Hutchinson
as a low-level staffer

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:35.400
who supposedly
had ulterior motives.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.300
-I spoke with some former
White House staffers,

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.400
three or four of them,
in the afternoon,

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:41.968
and they knew her well.

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:44.067
And not one person

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:47.434
had anything good to say
about her performance today.

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:50.801
-I would take their word over
any word of this junior staffer

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:52.334
who is completely,
I believe, lying

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:54.534
to the January 6th Committee
for her own self gain.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:57.534
-She wanted to work for Donald
Trump outside the White House

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:59.834
when he wasn't president
at Mar-A-Lago.

00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:03.467
-I'm not sure that any of this
is wholly out of character

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:06.033
with the Donald Trump
and the President Trump

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:07.467
that people came
to know over the years.

00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:09.434
-This committee
has come up with nothing

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:11.901
despite the fact
it's all one way.

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:14.200
-She's an extremely junior,
low-level aide.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.367
I don't think I ever had
a conversation with her.

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:18.868
-No, avoiding conversations
with Stephen Miller

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:20.734
is not proof
that you're a low-level aide.

00:03:20.734 --> 00:03:22.400
It's proof that
you're a human being

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.601
afraid of being eaten
Hannibal Lecter style.

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:28.000
No, of course. I don't
believe he's actually human.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.667
I think he's an enchanted doll
from a horror movie

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:32.634
that came to life
when a witch cast a spell

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:33.667
during a lightning storm.

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:35.100
Speaking of that,

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:38.000
has anyone seen my little
Stephen Miller doll?

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.901 --> 00:03:41.801
I swore I left him
on that chair.

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:44.133
[ Footsteps ]

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:46.868
Oh, no, no, no, no, no.
What are those footsteps?

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:48.901
Oh, God, no.

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:50.734
Little Stephen, no!

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:53.000
[ Thunder crashes ]

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.300
[ Witch cackling ]

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.868
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:02.067
-I mean, can you even imagine
trying to have a normal

00:04:02.067 --> 00:04:03.400
conversation
with Stephen Miller?

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.167
I've had nightmares where
I bump into him in the hallway

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:07.734
and have to
make small talk with him.

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:09.834
"Hey, Steve,
how about those Yankees?"

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:13.868
"They seem weak, vulnerable,
almost deliciously so."

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:15.767
"Cool. Cool, Steve.

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:17.667
I will catch you later."

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:20.067
Fox also tried
to discredit Hutchinson

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:22.968
by claiming she was just
testifying to get a TV gig.

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:25.133
-Well, it's like she was
auditioning for a seat

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:27.634
at "The View"
or "The Real Staffers

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.000
of Pennsylvania Avenue"
or something.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.767
It just seemed
like an audition tape.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:34.934
-You voted for a literal
reality show host for president.

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:37.567
Did you [bleep] just memory hole

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:39.000
the fact that before
he was president,

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.968
Trump spent most of his time
in a fake boardroom

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:44.467
yelling at Gene Simmons
and Lisa Rinna

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:47.400
over their
flailing hot dog business?

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.901
It was his last job
before president.

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:53.334
The Fox News spin
was so unconvincing

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:54.801
because the hearing itself
was so damning.

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:56.133
In many ways, the broad themes

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:57.567
were the same
as previous hearings.

00:04:57.567 --> 00:04:59.934
They all knew, Trump on down,
exactly what was happening.

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:01.067
They all knew it was illegal.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.467
They all knew
it could end in violence,

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:03.434
and they did it anyway.

00:05:03.434 --> 00:05:04.767
It was not a whim or impulse.

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:07.200
It was an orchestrated scheme
to overturn the election.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.634
And then when that failed,

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:11.200
incite a violent insurrection
to coerce Mike Pence

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.534
and Congress
into crowning Trump

00:05:13.534 --> 00:05:15.100
as an unelected autocrat.

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:16.868
For example,
Trump's direction of the mob

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:19.467
to march down to the Capitol
during his speech

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:21.567
was not
some spur-of-the-moment thing.

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:23.300
It was planned well in advance,

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.467
as Rudy Giuliani explained
to Hutchinson

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:27.667
in the conversation at
the White House on January 2nd,

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:29.801
four days before the riot,

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:32.634
where Rudy told her
that Chief of Staff Mark Meadows

00:05:32.634 --> 00:05:34.634
was involved in the plan,
as well.

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:37.033
-As Mr. Giuliani and I were
walking to his vehicles

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:40.400
that evening, he looked at me
and said something

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:43.901
to the effect of, "Cass,
are you excited for the 6th?

00:05:43.901 --> 00:05:46.067
It's going to be a great day."

00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:48.434
I remember looking at him
and saying, "Rudy,

00:05:48.434 --> 00:05:51.367
could you explain
what's happening on the 6th?"

00:05:51.367 --> 00:05:54.868
And he had responded something
to the effect of,

00:05:54.868 --> 00:05:57.901
"We're going to the Capitol.
It's going to be great.

00:05:57.901 --> 00:05:59.834
The president's
going to be there.

00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:01.300
He's going to look powerful.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:02.567
He's going to be
with the members.

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:04.000
He's going to be with
the senators.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.234
Talk to the chief about it.
Talk to the chief about it.

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:07.501
He knows about it."

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:09.901
-I like that Rudy talked
about a planned insurrection

00:06:09.901 --> 00:06:12.634
to overthrow democracy
with the same naive enthusiasm

00:06:12.634 --> 00:06:15.033
of a 6-year-old
who's going to the zoo.

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:16.334
"Did you hear?

00:06:16.334 --> 00:06:18.767
Mom's taking us to the reptile
exhibit on Thursday!

00:06:18.767 --> 00:06:21.767
She says there's an animal there
who looks just like me."

00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:24.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.234 --> 00:06:27.467
And, yeah, I know we use that
picture a lot, but so does he.

00:06:27.467 --> 00:06:29.200
We got it off his passport.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.767 --> 00:06:32.968
Of course, with Rudy, it's
hard to take anything he says

00:06:32.968 --> 00:06:35.667
at face value, given that
he could easily be confused.

00:06:35.667 --> 00:06:37.868
He seems like the kind of guy
who could be telling you

00:06:37.868 --> 00:06:40.200
a crazy story
and then halfway through stop

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:41.734
and say,
"Wait, no, I dreamed that.

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:43.334
That's right. I can't fly."

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:45.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.167 --> 00:06:47.868
So the plan all along was to
have Trump join the mob

00:06:47.868 --> 00:06:49.968
down at the Capitol,
which, suffice it to say,

00:06:49.968 --> 00:06:51.868
would have been horrifying
and impossible to contain,

00:06:51.868 --> 00:06:53.567
and Trump's cronies,
including Mark Meadows,

00:06:53.567 --> 00:06:55.934
knew that things could get ugly,
to say the least,

00:06:55.934 --> 00:06:58.234
and Meadows in particular
didn't really seem to care.

00:06:58.234 --> 00:07:00.834
-After Mr. Giuliani had
left the campus that evening,

00:07:00.834 --> 00:07:03.100
I went back up to our office

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:06.300
and I found Mr. Meadows
in his office on the couch.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.033
He was scrolling
through his phone.

00:07:08.033 --> 00:07:10.534
I remember leaning against
the doorway and saying,

00:07:10.534 --> 00:07:13.534
"I just had an interesting
conversation with Rudy, Mark.

00:07:13.534 --> 00:07:16.234
Sounds like we're going to
go to the Capitol."

00:07:16.234 --> 00:07:18.434
He didn't look up from his phone

00:07:18.434 --> 00:07:20.567
and said something
to the effect of,

00:07:20.567 --> 00:07:24.000
"There's a lot going on, Cass,
but I don't know.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.868
Things might get real,
real bad on January 6th."

00:07:27.868 --> 00:07:30.300
-He reacted to plans
for a violent coup

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:32.400
like an exhausted dad
who was just told

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.901
his kids are playing with a
bobcat they found in the woods.

00:07:35.901 --> 00:07:37.634
"They're fine.
There's three of them.

00:07:37.634 --> 00:07:40.267
I'm sure they can handle a cat.

00:07:40.267 --> 00:07:42.601
Kids, you okay out there?"

00:07:42.601 --> 00:07:46.133
[ Bobcat snarling,
clattering ]

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.868
Sounds like
they're having fun.

00:07:53.868 --> 00:07:56.000
So on the one hand,
as an unprecedented

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.334
Constitutional crisis
was unfolding,

00:07:57.334 --> 00:07:58.667
there were people
like Hutchinson

00:07:58.667 --> 00:08:00.601
who were at least paying
attention and asking questions.

00:08:00.601 --> 00:08:01.667
And then, on the other hand,

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:03.067
there were guys
like Mark Meadows

00:08:03.067 --> 00:08:04.734
who were just
totally [bleep] zonked

00:08:04.734 --> 00:08:06.200
and pretending
nothing was happening.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:08.100
Dude was just scrolling
on his phone,

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:09.167
ignoring pleas for help

00:08:09.167 --> 00:08:10.501
like a lifeguard
at a swimming pool

00:08:10.501 --> 00:08:12.000
who's got one guess left
in Wordle.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.267
"Stop your splashing.
I'm one letter away.

00:08:15.267 --> 00:08:16.767
Oh, sweet.

00:08:16.767 --> 00:08:18.400
Oh, no."

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:19.934
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.934 --> 00:08:23.300
So Trump's plan was to go
to the Capitol and lead the mob,

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:25.767
and Trump also knew
his supporters had weapons.

00:08:25.767 --> 00:08:27.400
In fact, when Trump found out
his supporters were being

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:28.767
denied access to his rally

00:08:28.767 --> 00:08:30.033
because they had weapons

00:08:30.033 --> 00:08:31.667
they couldn't bring
through the metal detectors

00:08:31.667 --> 00:08:33.901
known as magnetometers or mags,

00:08:33.901 --> 00:08:35.334
as you hear him say
in this clip,

00:08:35.334 --> 00:08:38.133
Trump said security should
let them keep the weapons

00:08:38.133 --> 00:08:41.834
so they could then march to
the Capitol with those weapons

00:08:41.834 --> 00:08:43.400
after his speech was over.

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:45.634
-I was in the vicinity of a
conversation where I overheard

00:08:45.634 --> 00:08:47.400
the president say something
to the effect of,

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:50.834
"You know, I don't effing care
that they have weapons.

00:08:50.834 --> 00:08:54.300
They're not here to hurt me.
Take the effing mags away.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.801
Let my people in. They can march
to the Capitol from here."

00:08:56.801 --> 00:08:58.400
-And just to be clear,

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:04.334
so he was told again
in that conversation

00:09:04.334 --> 00:09:05.934
or was he told again
in that conversation

00:09:05.934 --> 00:09:08.267
that people couldn't
come through the mags

00:09:08.267 --> 00:09:10.167
because they had weapons?
-Correct.

00:09:10.167 --> 00:09:13.567
-And that people --

00:09:13.567 --> 00:09:16.601
and his response was to say
they can march to the Capitol

00:09:16.601 --> 00:09:19.567
from the ellipse.

00:09:19.567 --> 00:09:22.901
-Something to the effect of
"take the," I think, "mags away.

00:09:22.901 --> 00:09:26.200
They're not here to hurt me.
Let them in. Let my people in.

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:28.367
They can march the Capitol
after the rally's over.

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:30.767
They can march from --
they can march from the ellipse.

00:09:30.767 --> 00:09:32.567
Take the effing mags away.

00:09:32.567 --> 00:09:35.100
Then they can march
to the Capitol."

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:36.334
-I mean, holy [bleep].

00:09:36.334 --> 00:09:38.133
It's been a day and a half
since I heard that,

00:09:38.133 --> 00:09:39.868
and I still can't
wrap my head around it.

00:09:39.868 --> 00:09:41.734
The president was told his
supporters were armed

00:09:41.734 --> 00:09:43.434
and said, "Let them in anyway."

00:09:43.434 --> 00:09:45.501
They can march to the Capitol
with their weapons,

00:09:45.501 --> 00:09:46.968
where their goal will be

00:09:46.968 --> 00:09:48.400
to overturn
the presidential election

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.467
and install him
as an unelected autocrat.

00:09:50.467 --> 00:09:53.100
You know what? Can we -- Let's
get that card back up, Wally.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:57.334
[ Laughter ]

00:09:57.334 --> 00:09:59.334
You know, it occurs to me

00:09:59.334 --> 00:10:02.334
that that card will be blurred
out for the viewers at home.

00:10:02.334 --> 00:10:06.334
So just so they know,
it says [bleep].

00:10:06.334 --> 00:10:08.968
I really don't know what to do

00:10:08.968 --> 00:10:10.868
with all the information
we learned yesterday

00:10:10.868 --> 00:10:12.367
other than to just sit with it,

00:10:12.367 --> 00:10:14.200
which brings us to a new segment
called

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:17.734
"Seth Just Has to Sit With It
for A Sec."

00:10:17.734 --> 00:10:21.000
[ Light laughter ]

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.801
[ Laughter ]

00:10:22.801 --> 00:10:25.033
I mean, God damn.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.200
[ Laughter ]

00:10:38.234 --> 00:10:39.667
[ Chuckles ]

00:10:39.667 --> 00:10:41.667
[ Laughter ]

00:10:44.634 --> 00:10:45.634
I mean...

00:10:45.634 --> 00:10:47.200
[ Laughter ]

00:10:49.167 --> 00:10:50.467
[ Laughs ]

00:10:50.467 --> 00:10:52.133
[ Laughter ]

00:10:55.767 --> 00:10:56.934
I mean...

00:10:56.934 --> 00:11:02.000
[ Laughter ]

00:11:07.834 --> 00:11:10.467
This has been "Seth Just Has to
Sit With It for A Sec."

00:11:10.467 --> 00:11:12.200
♪♪

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:18.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:18.133 --> 00:11:19.934
And Trump was apparently furious

00:11:19.934 --> 00:11:21.934
when he found out
he couldn't go to the Capitol.

00:11:21.934 --> 00:11:23.267
In fact, Hutchinson testified

00:11:23.267 --> 00:11:25.434
that he actually tried to
commandeer his own vehicle.

00:11:25.434 --> 00:11:26.868
Now, since her testimony
yesterday,

00:11:26.868 --> 00:11:29.033
two of the people involved,
Trump allies Bobby Engel

00:11:29.033 --> 00:11:31.968
and Tony Ornato, whose names
you'll hear often in the clip,

00:11:31.968 --> 00:11:33.767
have contested aspects
of the story

00:11:33.767 --> 00:11:35.801
through anonymous intermediaries
in the press,

00:11:35.801 --> 00:11:37.801
although I'm personally
skeptical of their denials,

00:11:37.801 --> 00:11:38.968
since for one thing,

00:11:38.968 --> 00:11:40.968
they weren't the ones
under oath, she was.

00:11:40.968 --> 00:11:42.968
And also, according to a
"Washington Post" reporter

00:11:42.968 --> 00:11:45.267
who has covered the secret
service extensively,

00:11:45.267 --> 00:11:48.267
Engel and Ornato were apparently
known as "enablers and 'yes men'

00:11:48.267 --> 00:11:49.667
to the president...
and very much people

00:11:49.667 --> 00:11:52.767
who wanted to do what he wanted
and see him pleased.

00:11:52.767 --> 00:11:55.767
So, both of those individuals
lose a little credibility

00:11:55.767 --> 00:11:57.634
because of
how closely they've been seen

00:11:57.634 --> 00:11:58.901
as aligned to Donald Trump."

00:11:58.901 --> 00:12:01.000
Obviously,
we'll need more information,

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:02.634
but the core of the story,
that Trump wanted to go

00:12:02.634 --> 00:12:03.901
to the Capitol and lead the mob

00:12:03.901 --> 00:12:05.767
and was irate when he couldn't,
is uncontested.

00:12:05.767 --> 00:12:08.634
Here's how Hutchinson
relayed it under oath yesterday.

00:12:08.634 --> 00:12:10.534
-Tony described him
as being irate.

00:12:12.734 --> 00:12:15.167
The president said something
to the effect of,

00:12:15.167 --> 00:12:19.467
"I'm the effing president.
Take me up to the Capitol now."

00:12:19.467 --> 00:12:21.133
To which Bobby responded,

00:12:21.133 --> 00:12:25.100
"Sir, we have to go back
to the West wing."

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:27.701
The president reached up

00:12:27.701 --> 00:12:30.734
towards the front of the vehicle
to grab at the steering wheel.

00:12:32.234 --> 00:12:35.234
Mr. Engel grabbed his arm, said,

00:12:35.234 --> 00:12:37.834
"Sir, you need to take your hand
off the steering wheel.

00:12:37.834 --> 00:12:40.801
We're going back
to the West wing.

00:12:40.801 --> 00:12:43.734
We're not going to the Capitol."

00:12:43.734 --> 00:12:45.901
Mr. Trump then used
his free hand

00:12:45.901 --> 00:12:47.801
to lunge towards Bobby Engel,

00:12:47.801 --> 00:12:50.968
and when Mr. Ornato
had recounted this story to me,

00:12:50.968 --> 00:12:53.400
he had motioned
towards his clavicles.

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:54.434
-My favorite part of this story

00:12:54.434 --> 00:12:55.767
is imagining
what would have happened

00:12:55.767 --> 00:12:57.534
if Trump had actually succeeded

00:12:57.534 --> 00:12:58.834
and gotten his hands
on the wheel.

00:12:58.834 --> 00:13:01.100
I mean, can you imagine him
driving a car?

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:03.334
I mean, we've seen him
drive a golf cart,

00:13:03.334 --> 00:13:05.501
but could he handle a, you know,
a steering wheel

00:13:05.501 --> 00:13:07.634
that doesn't come
with a tiny pencil holder?

00:13:07.634 --> 00:13:08.934
I mean, remember

00:13:08.934 --> 00:13:10.601
the one time he sat in
the driver's seat of a truck

00:13:10.601 --> 00:13:15.467
and handled the wheel like
a fifth-grader in a bumper car?

00:13:15.467 --> 00:13:18.367
Let's say he really did
get his hands on the wheel

00:13:18.367 --> 00:13:19.167
and drove the car.

00:13:19.167 --> 00:13:20.367
What would that look like?

00:13:20.367 --> 00:13:21.934
"Alright, hands at 10:00
and 2:00,

00:13:21.934 --> 00:13:25.400
adjust your mirrors,
check your blind spots,

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:27.901
turn signal on,
and we crashed into a tree.

00:13:27.901 --> 00:13:30.334
Guys, you got to tell the cops

00:13:30.334 --> 00:13:32.434
a cat ran out
and I swerved to save the cat.

00:13:32.434 --> 00:13:33.767
I can't get another ticket

00:13:33.767 --> 00:13:35.434
or they're going to
take my license away.

00:13:35.434 --> 00:13:38.000
And Mel already told me she
won't drive me anywhere.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.734
You got to get my back, guys."

00:13:40.734 --> 00:13:41.901
We've said this a lot

00:13:41.901 --> 00:13:43.467
over the entirety
of Trump's political career,

00:13:43.467 --> 00:13:45.033
but this hearing
really was shocking.

00:13:45.033 --> 00:13:46.167
I genuinely do not think

00:13:46.167 --> 00:13:47.567
I had the capacity
to be shocked anymore.

00:13:47.567 --> 00:13:49.601
Even Fox News seemed dazed
and paralyzed

00:13:49.601 --> 00:13:51.000
by how devastating it was.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.133
The president and his team
orchestrated a violent coup,

00:13:53.133 --> 00:13:54.534
and at every step of the way,

00:13:54.534 --> 00:13:57.300
they were aware of what they
were doing, that it was illegal,

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:58.467
and that it could lead
to violence.

00:13:58.467 --> 00:14:00.767
Trump wanted
to lead an armed mob

00:14:00.767 --> 00:14:01.968
to overturn the election.

00:14:01.968 --> 00:14:04.334
At this point,
we don't need any more evidence.

00:14:04.334 --> 00:14:06.234
We need the Justice Department
to act on it.

00:14:06.234 --> 00:14:09.501
In the meantime, we're all
just waiting around like this.

00:14:11.267 --> 00:14:15.534
[ Laughter ]

00:14:15.534 --> 00:14:16.901
This has been "A Closer Look."

